 ## What gets fixed for you
-Reported under "fixed" (read it, and write it that way next time): node names models often use (Lerp is LinearInterpolate, Mul is Multiply, TexCoord is TextureCoordinate), pin names (Edge0 / Edge1 / X on SmoothStep, X / Y on A / B nodes, T on a Lerp), a float4 meeting a float3, a float2 going where a float3 is needed (appended with 0), a channel picked from a one-output node ("n.R" - masked out), a color going into Opacity, Opacity outside 0..1 (Saturate), BaseColor in a UI material (it is FinalColor), Opacity in a Masked material (OpacityMask), a Noise with no Position, a library function's UV left unwired, a Custom node's code without return, the same parameter made twice, and unused nodes.
+Reported under "fixed" (read it, and write it that way next time): node names models often use (Lerp is LinearInterpolate, Mul is Multiply, TexCoord is TextureCoordinate), pin names (Edge0 / Edge1 / X on SmoothStep, X / Y on A / B nodes, T on a Lerp), a float4 meeting a float3, a float2 going where a float3 is needed (appended with 0), a SmoothStep with a constant Min above Max (it only rises in Unreal: swapped, OneMinus after), a channel picked from a one-output node ("n.R" - masked out), a color going into Opacity, Opacity outside 0..1 (Saturate), BaseColor in a UI material (it is FinalColor), Opacity in a Masked material (OpacityMask), a Noise with no Position, a library function's UV left unwired, a Custom node's code without return, the same parameter made twice, and unused nodes.
 
 ## When a build fails
 Graph problems: nothing was built - fix every listed problem and call again. Compile problems: the material was made; each error names the node (inside a macro: "g/d (inside g)") with a hint - fix and call build_ui_material again with material set to rebuild it in place. A Custom node (HLSL) is the escape hatch for dense maths: {id, type: "Custom", code: "return saturate(1 - length(uv - 0.5) * 2);", output: "float1", inputs: {uv: "$uv"}} - the inputs are the code's variable names.
